WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.176
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:01.176 --> 00:00:03.790
SPEAKER: Welcome to this
episode of "Click to Deploy,"

00:00:03.790 --> 00:00:05.860
the series where we
show you how easy it

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:09.850
is to deploy solutions from
the Google Cloud Marketplace.

00:00:09.850 --> 00:00:11.770
In this episode,
we'll be reviewing

00:00:11.770 --> 00:00:14.620
how to set up a LAMP stack
through the marketplace.

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:20.110
LAMP stands for Linux operating
system, Apache HTTP server,

00:00:20.110 --> 00:00:23.920
MySQL database management
system, and PHP programming

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:24.760
language.

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:26.590
It's a set of
open-source software

00:00:26.590 --> 00:00:29.770
used to build web applications.

00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:32.130
We'll start by searching
for "LAMP stack" in the GCP

00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:32.970
Marketplace.

00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:35.280
There are a few options
from different vendors,

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:38.070
each with their own version
of Linux, differing security

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:40.920
models, as well
as support models.

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:43.740
For this demo, we'll choose the
Google Click to Deploy option.

00:00:47.650 --> 00:00:50.840
Let's do a quick run-through of
the summary of the deployment.

00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:53.770
This specific deployment will
be launched on a single VM

00:00:53.770 --> 00:00:55.870
of my size choosing.

00:00:55.870 --> 00:00:57.880
As always, the
pricing information

00:00:57.880 --> 00:01:01.040
displays a high-level
estimate of charges.

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:02.720
Once we customize
our deployment,

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:05.332
we'll receive a more
detailed breakdown.

00:01:05.332 --> 00:01:06.290
Let's start the launch.

00:01:09.190 --> 00:01:11.650
Similar to many marketplace
deployment options,

00:01:11.650 --> 00:01:14.860
we'll pick a name and the
zone in which we'll deploy.

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:18.910
I'll stick with the default
name and zone, US West 2B.

00:01:18.910 --> 00:01:20.920
We can also continue
with the default machine

00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:22.990
type, which is an
E2 small, having

00:01:22.990 --> 00:01:26.020
two VCPUs and 2 gigs of memory.

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:28.780
Let's keep the default for boot
disk and networking options.

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:36.300
We'll end with making sure our
VM can accept HTTP and HTTPS

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:37.550
traffic from the internet.

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:45.180
Before you deploy, you can
see a final estimate of costs

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:48.240
with the custom options you
configured for deployment.

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:51.570
By clicking Details, you can
expand for an itemized cost

00:01:51.570 --> 00:01:52.830
breakdown.

00:01:52.830 --> 00:01:54.720
Keep in mind,
these costs may not

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:58.770
include charges for
networking and monitoring.

00:01:58.770 --> 00:02:00.840
We'll launch and give
it a minute to spin up.

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:08.699
Let's take a look at our
deployment information.

00:02:08.699 --> 00:02:11.510
Clicking the site address will
display our default LAMP web

00:02:11.510 --> 00:02:12.787
application.

00:02:12.787 --> 00:02:14.495
This is just the
landing page for Apache.

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:21.650
One of the first
suggested next steps

00:02:21.650 --> 00:02:23.825
is to change the MySQL
temporary password.

00:02:27.220 --> 00:02:30.630
So we can do that by using
the PHP My Admin web interface

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:31.740
that's provided to us.

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:45.000
Now that we're more
secure, let's go back

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.400
and change our landing
page to something custom.

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:50.670
We can SSH into the VM
and act as the root user

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:53.190
to customize the
index.html page.

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:11.810
We can refresh our
IP URL, and now we

00:03:11.810 --> 00:03:14.440
have our very simple,
yet customized, LAMP

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:17.390
stack deployed at the click of
a button using the Google Cloud

00:03:17.390 --> 00:03:19.590
Marketplace.

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:21.920
If you enjoyed this video,
please subscribe and hit

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:23.360
the Like button below.

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:25.790
We encourage you to check
out the GCP Marketplace

00:03:25.790 --> 00:03:27.720
and deploy this
solution on your own.

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:28.610
Thanks for watching.

00:03:28.610 --> 00:03:31.660
[MUSIC PLAYING]

